  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Colossal Contracting obligated $232M in FY2026 to date. Colossal Contracting won 551 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $421K, and obligations are up 17.7% year over year. Colossal Contracting recorded $413M in FY21, $342M in FY22, $128M in FY23, $183M in FY24, and $197M in FY25 before reaching $232M in FY26. Colossal Contracting’s top buying agency in FY2026 to date is the Social Security Administration with $54M, followed by the Department of Agriculture with $35.5M and the Department of the Interior with $24.9M. Colossal Contracting’s largest NAICS market is Other Computer Related Services with $184M, with Telephone Apparatus Manufacturing second at $46.2M and Computer Systems Design Services at $906K. This summary highlights where obligations are concentrated across agencies and markets during the current fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Colossal Contracting’s contracting trended over recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "Colossal Contracting obligated $413M in FY21, $342M in FY22, $128M in FY23, $183M in FY24, $197M in FY25, and $232M in FY26 to date. Colossal Contracting’s FY2026 obligations are up 17.7% year over year. Colossal Contracting’s award count for FY2026 to date is 551, with an average award size of $421K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are Colossal Contracting’s top customers and what markets do they buy?",
        "body": "The Social Security Administration is Colossal Contracting’s largest buyer in FY2026 to date with $54M, followed by the Department of Agriculture with $35.5M and the Department of the Interior with $24.9M. Other major buyers include the Department of Veterans Affairs with $19.5M and the Department of Defense with $15.6M. Other Computer Related Services is Colossal Contracting’s largest market with $184M, and Telephone Apparatus Manufacturing is next with $46.2M."
      }
